prompt:
Create unit `tasks` and implement `clamp`: for lo <= hi, return x limited to the range [lo, hi]. The contract must state that the result lies in [lo, hi] and equals x whenever x is already in range.

Required signature (in unit `tasks`):
fn clamp(x: i64, lo: i64, hi: i64) -> (r: i64)

reference.code:
spec fn ordered(lo: i64, hi: i64) -> bool { lo <= hi }

spec fn clamped(x: i64, lo: i64, hi: i64, r: i64) -> bool { lo <= r && r <= hi && ((lo <= x && x <= hi) ==> r == x) }

#[effects(pure)]
#[uses(ordered, clamped)]
fn clamp(x: i64, lo: i64, hi: i64) -> (r: i64)
    requires ordered(lo, hi),
    ensures clamped(x, lo, hi, r),
{
    if x < lo { lo } else { if x > hi { hi } else { x } }
}

